{% comment %}
  Renders the storefront Custom Jewelry enquiry form (Slice 9, README
  "Custom Jewelry -- MVP1 Locked Direction"). POSTs to
  `POST /apps/carat/custom-jewelry-intake`
  (app/app/routes/apps.carat.custom-jewelry-intake.tsx) via
  `assets/custom-jewelry-intake-form.js` -- a plain `<form>`, NOT Shopify's
  native `{% form %}` tag, because there is no native Shopify form type for a
  custom App Proxy submission. Field/error markup follows
  `sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid` closely: `.field`/`.field__input`/
  `.field__label`/`.field--with-error` and `.form-status`/`.form__message`
  are EXISTING Dawn classes reused here, not reinvented.

  COPY STATUS -- read before editing any string in this file or its locale
  keys. TWO strings are OWNER-APPROVED and evidence-pinned, not draft:

    `.confirmation_template`  -- the post-submission confirmation
    `.deposit_disclosure`     -- the $49 Design Deposit disclosure

  Both are imported byte-for-byte from
  `app/app/domain/customjewelry/intakeCopy.ts`
  (`CUSTOM_JEWELRY_INTAKE_CONFIRMATION_TEMPLATE` /
  `CUSTOM_JEWELRY_DESIGN_DEPOSIT_DISCLOSURE`) and proven identical by
  `app/app/theme/ownerApprovedCopy.test.ts`. The two follow-up choice labels
  are owner-approved too, pinned in `intakeCopy.test.ts`. EVERY OTHER string
  in this file's locale keys -- the intro, the field labels, the errors -- is
  mechanical form furniture, drafted here, carrying no promise.

  ============================================================================
  THIS FORM RENDERS FOR SIGNED-OUT VISITORS. THAT IS THE DECISION.
  ============================================================================
  Unlike `warranty-claim-form.liquid`, which hides everything behind a
  sign-in gate, this form is fully usable with no account -- an explicit owner
  decision (2026-10-05): "do not force account creation merely to submit the
  enquiry". The README calls the initial request "free and intentionally
  low-friction", and `docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` requires an account
  for every PURCHASE path; a pre-purchase enquiry is not one.

  WHAT *IS* GATED is the upload control, and only that. A signed-out visitor
  sees the inspiration-links textarea plus a sign-in invitation in place of
  the file input -- never a file input that cannot work. The reason is abuse
  and storage, not payment: an endpoint minting presigned PUTs for anyone is
  free file hosting on our account.

  THE DEPOSIT DISCLOSURE IS ALWAYS VISIBLE, never behind a toggle or a
  "learn more". It is the first thing after the intro, because "this enquiry
  is free" must be something the customer can rely on before they hand over
  their details rather than something they discover afterwards.

  NO ABANDONMENT / NON-RESPONSE RULE ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE. Owner instruction,
  verbatim: "Do not put the abandonment/non-response rule on the initial
  intake form. Keep the intake welcoming." It is not dropped -- it must appear
  conspicuously on the deposit/design-approval step, where the customer
  affirmatively accepts it before any money moves. `intakeCopy.test.ts`
  asserts the disclosure does not carry it.

  NO RESPONSE-TIME PROMISE ANYWHERE. Not "shortly", not "as soon as
  possible" -- the owner struck that kind of phrasing from the warranty copy
  twice and from this surface explicitly.

  NO PAYMENT HERE. No price field, no deposit charge, no checkout. The route
  takes no payment input and the table it writes has no payment columns; the
  README is explicit that intake must not charge the deposit yet.

  CLIENT-SIDE VALIDATION IS UX, NOT ENFORCEMENT -- the same division of
  labour `warranty-claim-form.liquid` and `bank-payment-checkout-dialog
  .liquid` describe. The authority is the Zod schema and the 401/422 branches
  in the route.

  Accepts (schema settings): heading (optional override).
{% endcomment %}
{{ 'component-custom-jewelry-intake-form.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="page-width page-width--narrow section-{{ section.id }}-padding carat-custom-jewelry">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="title title-wrapper--no-top-margin {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
        {{ section.settings.heading }}
      </h2>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Visually hidden when unset, matching contact-form.liquid and
        warranty-claim-form.liquid -- `sections/main-page.liquid` (rendered
        first in templates/page.custom-jewelry.json) already shows the
        Shopify page's own title as an <h1>, so a second VISIBLE heading
        would duplicate it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h2 class="visually-hidden">{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.heading' | t }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__intro">
      {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.intro' | t -}}
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      OWNER-APPROVED, ALWAYS VISIBLE, FIRST. See this file's header comment on
      why it is not behind a toggle.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__deposit-notice" role="note">
      <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__deposit-text">
        {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.deposit_disclosure' | t -}}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      id="CustomJewelryErrorSummary"
      class="carat-custom-jewelry__error-summary form-status-list"
      role="alert"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
      data-carat-cj-error-summary
    ></div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The OWNER-APPROVED confirmation sentence is carried as a data attribute
      rather than built in JS, so the string lives in exactly one place: the
      locale file, pinned against
      `app/app/domain/customjewelry/intakeCopy.ts` by
      `app/app/theme/ownerApprovedCopy.test.ts`. The JS substitutes
      `{projectReference}` with the reference the SERVER assigned — never a
      value the browser invented.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      id="CustomJewelryConfirmation"
      class="carat-custom-jewelry__confirmation"
      role="status"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
      data-carat-cj-confirmation
      data-confirmation-template="{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.confirmation_template' | t | escape }}"
    ></div>

    <form id="CustomJewelryIntakeForm" novalidate data-carat-cj-form>
      <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-row">
        <div class="field field--with-error">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="CustomJewelryFirstName"
            name="first_name"
            class="field__input"
            autocomplete="given-name"
            required
            value="{{ customer.first_name | escape }}"
            aria-describedby="CustomJewelryFirstName-error"
          >
          <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryFirstName">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.first_name_label' | t }}
            <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
          >
          <small
            id="CustomJewelryFirstName-error"
            class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-cj-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="field field--with-error">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="CustomJewelryLastName"
            name="last_name"
            class="field__input"
            autocomplete="family-name"
            required
            value="{{ customer.last_name | escape }}"
            aria-describedby="CustomJewelryLastName-error"
          >
          <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryLastName">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.last_name_label' | t }}
            <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
          >
          <small
            id="CustomJewelryLastName-error"
            class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-cj-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-row">
        <div class="field field--with-error">
          <input
            type="email"
            id="CustomJewelryEmail"
            name="email"
            class="field__input"
            autocomplete="email"
            spellcheck="false"
            autocapitalize="off"
            required
            value="{{ customer.email | escape }}"
            aria-describedby="CustomJewelryEmail-error"
          >
          <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryEmail">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.email_label' | t }}
            <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
          >
          <small
            id="CustomJewelryEmail-error"
            class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-cj-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>

        <div class="field field--with-error">
          <input
            type="tel"
            id="CustomJewelryPhone"
            name="phone"
            class="field__input"
            autocomplete="tel"
            required
            aria-describedby="CustomJewelryPhone-error"
          >
          <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryPhone">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.phone_label' | t }}
            <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
          >
          <small
            id="CustomJewelryPhone-error"
            class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
            hidden
            data-carat-cj-field-error
          >
            <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
            <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="carat-custom-jewelry__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-custom-jewelry__legend">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.starting_point_legend' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </legend>
        <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio-group carat-custom-jewelry__radio-group--stacked">
          <label class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="starting_point" value="from_scratch" required data-carat-cj-starting-point>
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.starting_point_from_scratch' | t -}}
          </label>
          <label class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="starting_point" value="existing_design" required data-carat-cj-starting-point>
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.starting_point_existing_design' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
        <small
          id="CustomJewelryStartingPoint-error"
          class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-cj-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <textarea
          id="CustomJewelryPrompt"
          name="prompt_text"
          class="text-area field__input"
          rows="6"
          required
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.prompt_placeholder' | t }}"
          aria-describedby="CustomJewelryPrompt-error"
        ></textarea>
        <label class="form__label field__label" for="CustomJewelryPrompt">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.prompt_label' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label
        >
        <small
          id="CustomJewelryPrompt-error"
          class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-cj-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <input
          type="text"
          id="CustomJewelryType"
          name="jewelry_type"
          class="field__input"
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.jewelry_type_placeholder' | t }}"
        >
        <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryType">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.jewelry_type_label' | t -}}
        </label>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        BUDGET. Optional, and submitted as a STRING of minor units -- the
        route's schema rejects a JSON number for it, because a budget is money
        and a JSON number is an IEEE double. The customer types dollars; the
        JS converts to integer cents without floating-point arithmetic (see
        `dollarsToMinorUnits` there). Currency is fixed to the only one MVP1
        sells in; it is submitted explicitly because the route requires both
        halves of a budget or neither.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="field field--with-error">
        <input
          type="text"
          id="CustomJewelryBudget"
          name="approximate_budget"
          class="field__input"
          inputmode="decimal"
          autocomplete="off"
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.budget_placeholder' | t }}"
          aria-describedby="CustomJewelryBudget-help CustomJewelryBudget-error"
        >
        <label class="field__label" for="CustomJewelryBudget">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.budget_label' | t -}}
        </label>
        <small id="CustomJewelryBudget-help" class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-help">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.budget_help' | t -}}
        </small>
        <small
          id="CustomJewelryBudget-error"
          class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-cj-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        TIMING. "No deadline" and a date are two answers to one question, and
        the route refuses both together -- so the JS clears and disables the
        date input while the checkbox is ticked rather than letting the
        customer assemble a request the server will reject.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <fieldset class="carat-custom-jewelry__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-custom-jewelry__legend">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.timing_legend' | t -}}
        </legend>
        <div class="field">
          <label class="field__label field__label--static" for="CustomJewelryDesiredDate">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.desired_date_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input
            type="date"
            id="CustomJewelryDesiredDate"
            name="desired_completion_date"
            class="field__input"
            data-carat-cj-desired-date
          >
        </div>
        <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__control">
          <input
            type="checkbox"
            id="CustomJewelryNoDeadline"
            name="has_no_deadline"
            class="carat-custom-jewelry__checkbox"
            data-carat-cj-no-deadline
          >
          <label for="CustomJewelryNoDeadline" class="carat-custom-jewelry__checkbox-label">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.no_deadline_label' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      {%- comment -%}
        INSPIRATION. Two ways in, deliberately, and the first works with no
        account at all -- the owner asked for a plain-text links field
        precisely so a signed-out visitor is not pushed into registering.

        NOTHING SERVER-SIDE EVER FETCHES THESE LINKS. A server that retrieves
        a customer-supplied URL is an SSRF primitive; staff open them in a
        browser, where they are ordinary untrusted links. The route's own
        module comment says the same.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <fieldset class="carat-custom-jewelry__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-custom-jewelry__legend">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.inspiration_legend' | t -}}
        </legend>
        <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__help">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.inspiration_help' | t -}}
        </p>

        <div class="field">
          <textarea
            id="CustomJewelryInspirationLinks"
            name="inspiration_links"
            class="text-area field__input"
            rows="3"
            placeholder="{{ 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.inspiration_links_placeholder' | t }}"
          ></textarea>
          <label class="form__label field__label" for="CustomJewelryInspirationLinks">
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.inspiration_links_label' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>

        {%- if customer -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            UPLOADS -- authenticated visitors only, and this is a server-side
            render-time branch on Liquid's own `customer` object, not a
            client-side hide-after-render.

            PHOTOS ONLY in this iteration, for the same reason as the warranty
            form: the checksum the server requires is computed in the browser,
            and hashing a 300 MB video in a phone tab is a hang waiting to
            happen. The 20 MB photo ceiling keeps it bounded.

            Hidden until the JS confirms storage is available, then revealed.
            If the destination endpoint reports storage unavailable the control
            stays hidden and `uploads_note` appears instead -- the customer is
            never left with a file input that silently does nothing, and the
            note names no internal cause.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__uploads" data-carat-cj-uploads hidden>
            <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__help" id="carat-cj-uploads-help">
              {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.uploads_help' | t -}}
            </p>
            <input
              type="file"
              class="carat-custom-jewelry__file-input"
              accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/heic,image/heif"
              multiple
              aria-describedby="carat-cj-uploads-help"
              data-carat-cj-upload-input
            >
            <ul class="carat-custom-jewelry__upload-list" data-carat-cj-upload-list></ul>
            <small
              class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
              hidden
              data-carat-cj-upload-error
              role="status"
            >
              <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
              <span data-carat-cj-upload-error-text></span>
            </small>
          </div>

          <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__uploads-note" data-carat-cj-uploads-unavailable hidden>
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.uploads_note' | t -}}
          </p>
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            THE ONLY GATED THING ON THIS PAGE. An invitation, not a wall: the
            rest of the form above and below remains fully usable, and the
            sign-in link returns the visitor to this exact page. The sentence
            itself is the owner-approved gate wording from
            `docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` §4, reused verbatim so every
            gate in the storefront reads identically.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__uploads-signin" data-carat-cj-uploads-signin>
            <p class="carat-custom-jewelry__uploads-signin-message">
              {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.uploads_sign_in_message' | t -}}
            </p>
            <a
              href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ request.path | url_encode }}"
              class="link carat-custom-jewelry__uploads-signin-link"
            >
              {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.uploads_sign_in_link' | t -}}
            </a>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset class="carat-custom-jewelry__fieldset">
        <legend class="carat-custom-jewelry__legend">
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.follow_up_legend' | t }}
          <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </legend>
        {%- comment -%}
          The two OWNER-APPROVED choices, in the approved order. Their values
          are the contract with `custom_jewelry_project.follow_up_preference`
          and are pinned alongside the labels in `intakeCopy.test.ts`.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio-group carat-custom-jewelry__radio-group--stacked">
          <label class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio">
            <input
              type="radio"
              name="follow_up_preference"
              value="schedule_consultation"
              required
              data-carat-cj-follow-up
            >
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.follow_up_schedule_consultation' | t -}}
          </label>
          <label class="carat-custom-jewelry__radio">
            <input type="radio" name="follow_up_preference" value="contact_me" required data-carat-cj-follow-up>
            {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.follow_up_contact_me' | t -}}
          </label>
        </div>
        <small
          id="CustomJewelryFollowUp-error"
          class="carat-custom-jewelry__field-error form__message"
          hidden
          data-carat-cj-field-error
        >
          <span class="svg-wrapper">{{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}</span>
          <span data-carat-cj-field-error-text></span>
        </small>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="carat-custom-jewelry__actions">
        <button type="submit" class="button" data-carat-cj-submit>
          {{- 'templates.custom_jewelry.form.submit' | t -}}
        </button>
      </div>

      <p
        id="CustomJewelryStatus"
        class="carat-custom-jewelry__status form-status"
        role="status"
        aria-live="polite"
        hidden
        data-carat-cj-status
      ></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'custom-jewelry-intake-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Custom jewelry form",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h2", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "h1", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "h0", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "h1",
      "label": "Heading size"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Custom jewelry form"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
